commit 3783e830dae165c0e1f2c781c5f70be172a11df9
Author: seekskyworld <djh1813553759@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 30 01:42:04 2026 +0800

    W4: check interrupts after the opcode fetch (Mooneye 41 -> 42: rapid_toggle)

    Hardware fetches the next opcode in the last M-cycle of an instruction and only then checks
    IME && IE&IF; with D002 (peripherals before access) an interrupt raised by a peripheral in the
    fetch M-cycle must therefore preempt that instruction. step() now fetches, then checks; on
    dispatch the fetched opcode is discarded and PC steps back 1 (after a HALT bug this lands on
    the HALT itself, Pan Docs halt.md), and the fetch counts as dispatch M-cycle 1 of 5
    (fetch, idle, PCH, PCL, idle). HALT: each halted M-cycle is a fetch at PC without increment;
    on wake with IME=1 that fetch is dispatch M-cycle 1, with IME=0 the fetched opcode executes,
    so HALT waiting keeps exactly the timing of a NOP loop.

    gates G1 12/12 G2 1/1 G3 4/4 G4 0/1 (PPU stub), SST 500/500, cargo test --workspace green;
    Mooneye scan: rapid_toggle FAIL -> PASS, no other change.

